# Build-context allowlist. The build context is the repository root, which holds
# the real .env, the working database, the legacy-data tree, and node_modules --
# gigabytes of material no image needs, and credentials no image may see. Ignore
# everything, then re-admit only the paths the Dockerfiles actually COPY, so a
# new file at the repo root cannot silently enter a build context.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!src
!ifpa
